{ name: 'Branson Shenanigans RV Park', where: '3675 Keeter St · Branson, MO', city: 'Branson, MO', phone: '(417) 334-1920', tag: 'Campground', facts: ['Full hookups, 30/50 amp'], note: 'Wooded, quiet park minutes from the Branson Strip. Dog park on site.', source: 'Biscuit researched this', zip: '65616', lat: 36.671, lng: -93.249 },
{ name: 'Lake Jacomo Campground (Fleming Park)', where: 'Fleming Park, Lee\'s Summit, MO 64064', city: 'Kansas City, MO', phone: '(816) 503-4805', tag: 'County Park', facts: ['Mix of full-hookup sites (water/electric/sewer) and electric-only primitive sites, with 20/30/50-amp service available', 'Dogs welcome on leash throughout the campground and grassy sites', 'Seasonal - open March through October 31; about 17-20 minutes from downtown KC'], note: 'This is one of my favorite close-to-town spots - big grassy pads to stretch my legs, a lake nearby for splashing, and it\'s basically in Kansas City\'s backyard. Just remember it closes up for winter, so it\'s a warm-weather pick.', source: 'Biscuit researched this', zip: '64064', lat: 38.983, lng: -94.343 },
{ name: 'Kansas City East / Oak Grove KOA Holiday', where: '303 NE 3rd St, Oak Grove, MO 64075', city: 'Kansas City, MO', phone: '(816) 690-6660', tag: 'RV Park', facts: ['Full-hookup RV sites with 30-amp and 50-amp electric, pull-throughs up to 80 feet', 'Dogs allowed but must stay leashed (6 ft max) whenever outside your rig', 'About 22 minutes east of downtown Kansas City off I-70'], note: 'A KOA is always a safe bet when you want reliable hookups and good amenities without fuss, and this one\'s an easy, paw-friendly hop off the interstate on your way through KC.', source: 'Biscuit researched this', zip: '64075', lat: 39.000, lng: -94.145 },
{ name: 'Watkins Mill State Park Campground', where: '26600 Park Rd N, Lawson, MO 64062', city: 'Kansas City, MO', phone: '1-877-422-6766', tag: 'State Park', facts: ['96 campsites, 74 with electric hookups including 50-amp sites', 'Dogs must be on a leash no longer than 10 feet - no shock collars or portable fences count as restraint', 'About 30-35 minutes northeast of downtown Kansas City; some sites open year-round'], note: 'If you want real trees and a lake instead of a parking-lot vibe, this Missouri state park delivers - just bring an actual leash (not a fence or an e-collar) since the rules are specific about that, and check which loop stays open if you\'re visiting in winter.', source: 'Biscuit researched this', zip: '64062', lat: 39.456, lng: -94.178 },
{ name: 'St. Louis West / Historic Route 66 KOA Holiday', where: '18475 Old US Hwy 66, Eureka, MO 63025', city: 'St. Louis, MO', phone: '(636) 257-3018', tag: 'KOA', facts: ['Wooded, natural-feeling sites with RV/tent spots plus rental cabins', 'Leashed dogs are welcome throughout the campground', 'Sites are gravel (not paved) and some are sloped, so it can be a squeeze for very large rigs — call ahead on breed policy'], note: 'A shady, tree-covered KOA that feels more like real camping than a parking-lot RV park — good for letting a dog stretch its legs, just keep the leash on since it\'s a busy, family-heavy property.', source: 'Biscuit researched this', zip: '63025', lat: 38.491, lng: -90.616 },
{ name: '370 Lakeside Park', where: '1000 Lakeside Park Dr, St Peters, MO 63376', city: 'St. Louis, MO', phone: '(636) 387-5253', tag: 'RV Park', facts: ['Level concrete and gravel pull-through sites right around a scenic lake', 'On-site dog park plus a 4-mile lakeside walking/biking trail', 'About 30 minutes from downtown St. Louis'], note: 'One of the prettiest and best-maintained RV stops in the area — the lakeside trail and dedicated dog park make it an easy favorite for morning walks with your pup before a day in the city.', source: 'Biscuit researched this', zip: '63376', lat: 38.801, lng: -90.612 },
{ name: 'Meramec State Park', where: '115 Meramec Pk Rd, Sullivan, MO 63080', city: 'St. Louis, MO', phone: '(573) 468-6072', tag: 'State Park', facts: ['Large campground with electric sites, showers, an RV dump station, and a camp store', 'Leashed dogs are allowed on trails and in most of the campground — a few beach/swim areas restrict pets', 'River access for paddling plus miles of hiking trails through caves and bluffs'], note: 'A beautiful, more rugged escape from the city with real trails to explore together — just keep a leash handy, since Missouri state parks require pets to be leashed and some swim spots are off-limits to dogs.', source: 'Biscuit researched this', zip: '63080', lat: 38.214, lng: -91.078 },
{ name: 'Lake Ozarks RV Resort', where: '1726 State Hwy KK · Osage Beach, MO', city: 'Lake of the Ozarks, MO', phone: '(816) 629-1131', tag: 'RV Resort', facts: ['20/30/50 amp, pull-through & back-in', 'Dog park; 2 pets per site', 'RVs over 10 years old need approval'], note: 'Pet-friendly park about 2.5 miles from Osage Beach. Sites are gravel, not paved, so big Class A rigs should ask about leveling.', source: 'Biscuit researched this', zip: '65065', lat: 38.132, lng: -92.670 },
{ name: 'Lake of the Ozarks State Park', where: '403 Hwy 134 · Brumley, MO', city: 'Lake of the Ozarks, MO', phone: '(573) 348-2694', tag: 'State Park', facts: ['No published max RV length; confirm at booking', 'Basic, electric (incl. 50 amp) & full-hookup sites (Section 4)'], note: 'Missouri\'s largest state park, right on the lake. Up to 2 dogs per site on a leash of 10ft or less. Dogs aren\'t allowed on swim beaches.', source: 'Biscuit researched this', zip: '65017', lat: 38.092, lng: -92.495 },
{ name: 'Mark Twain Cave Campground', where: '300 Cave Hollow Rd · Hannibal, MO', city: 'Hannibal (Mark Twain country), MO', phone: '(573) 221-1656', tag: 'Campground', facts: ['Full hookups, 20/30/50-amp', 'Dog wash on site', 'Full services Apr-Oct'], note: 'About a mile from historic downtown Hannibal, next to the Mark Twain Cave and a winery. Sites are fairly close together. Pets welcome, no fee.', source: 'Biscuit researched this', zip: '63401', lat: 39.690, lng: -91.466 }
